    "reason": "Design rationale from sources (component_record id 260, excitation_record p4-bf-stretched-port-window-v1, model_law b-transient-behavior-v1). Fixed physics forces the choice: the latch is \"volatile\", so the press must be captured while ready (ready_v 2.8 V, boot_delay 1 ms) and then held continuously to TX; the single 40 uJ shunt at t=15 ms demands emax - 40 uJ >= eoff, i.e. C*(5.445-1.62) >= 40 uJ -> C >= ~10.5 uF, which the 10 uF default violates (emax 54.45 uJ < 40 + 16.2 uJ), so the shipped default cannot survive the shunt without a brownout that erases the volatile capture. Upper bound from contact_duration 0.01 s: eon = 3.92*C must be reachable before ~9 ms. C = 22 uF (permitted max) satisfies both: eon 86.24 uJ reached by 7.2 ms, emax 119.8 uJ, eoff 35.64 uJ. tx_not_before_s set at the permitted max 0.05625 s so the 28.8 uJ frame is sent when the second source segment has restored storage. Checked once (recorded observation, not a host label): boot 0.0072 s, capture 0.0082 s inside the 0-0.01 s contact, no brownout between capture and TX, TX start 0.0563 s, tx-complete 0.0582 s (< deadline 0.125 s), exactly one packet 010400010101b0260657 with 8 application bytes and loaded_v 2.3706 V >= output_v 1.8 V; ledger totals harvest 189 uJ, conversion 21 uJ, boot 5 uJ, shunt 40 uJ, tx 28.8 uJ, background 96.5 uJ, spill 0, bad_steps [], max balance error ~1e-20. The returned activity is a first-six-last-six projection, not a full trace; the brownout shown at 0.4043 s occurs after tx-complete and after source end, with event_was_captured false, so it cannot alter the delivered frame or cause duplicate transmission. Basis: frozen deterministic model only, source_calibration UNAVAILABLE and physical_qualification UNKNOWN; no hardware, statistical, transfer or self-improvement claim is made.",
